<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladimir the Bold</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1353–1410</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Vladimir Andreyevich of Serpukhov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladimir the Bold, Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serpukhov">Serpukhov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borovsk">Borovsk</a>, was a cousin of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-donskoy">Dmitry Donskoy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and his leading general. He commanded the reserve regiment that decided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kulikovo">Battle of Kulikovo</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in 1380, and he defended Moscow during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edigu">Edigu</a>'s raid of 1408.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-bold.jpg" alt="Vladimir the Bold" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Стенопись Архангельского собора Московского Кремля · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B7%D1%8C_%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%80_%D0%A5%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B1%D1%80%D1%8B%D0%B9,_%D0%A4%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%90%D1%80%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
